cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived release.
title: >-
  PAT-TBI Score: analysis code
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for the PAT-TBI score (Platelet Allocation Tool for
  Traumatic Brain Injury), an integer score that estimates the chance that an
  adult patient with traumatic brain injury receives a platelet transfusion
  within 4 hours of emergency department arrival. The score was derived and
  internally validated on the American College of Surgeons National Trauma
  Data Bank research data (admission years 2020 to 2024). The repository holds
  code only: no patient-level data, result tables or figures are included.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/samersalman/pat-tbi-score'
authors:
  - given-names: Samer G.
    family-names: Salman
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9897-4071'
    affiliation: 'Baylor College of Medicine'
keywords:
  - traumatic brain injury
  - platelet transfusion
  - trauma
  - clinical prediction rule
  - integer risk score
  - LASSO stability selection
  - National Trauma Data Bank
